x86-only: the test writes a value into the STM32 register window (0x4001xxxx) and reads it back through gpio-read/uart-recv/spi-transfer; under codex-vm that window is RAM, while the arm64/riscv beds have no device and no RAM there (a read answers 255, the floating-bus value). The lifecycle it proves is bed-independent and is what the errors/hal-tuple-* refusals pin on every lane.